Modified files and adaptations:
 src/openpi/models/mamba3/core.py: extract stateless SISO SSD, remove packed
 sequences, retain triangular/chunk math; explicitly highest-precision dot
 accumulation to meet FP32 tolerances on CUDA as well as CPU.
 src/openpi/models/mamba3/mixer.py: minimum SISO NNX wrapper for Flax 0.10.2;
 no LM, MIMO or carry cache; explicit compute dtype and FP32 sensitive math.
 src/openpi/models/mamba3/action_expert.py: Torch gated FiLM/FFN/time blocks
 ported to NNX; no cross-attention/history/early-exit variants.
 src/openpi/models/mamba3/context_compressor.py: masked integer-boundary pooling
 and global-query MHA ported to NNX with safe all-empty rows. All three camera
 streams participate in fixed base/left/right order, followed by all prompt
 slots (including discretized state text). No two-camera token slicing.

Verified hyperparameter correspondence (not a claim of paper reproduction):
 d_model/hidden_size=512, depth=4, d_state/state_size=64, expand=1,
 headdim/head_dim=64, chunk_size=64, is_mimo=false, ngroups=1,
 rope_fraction=.5, A_floor=1e-4, B/C RMS epsilon=1e-5, dt_min=.001,
 dt_max=.1, dt_init_floor=1e-4, is_outproj_norm=false, mixer bias=false,
 MHA heads=8, dropout=0, FFN=2048, FiLM hidden=2048, RMS epsilon=1e-6,
 vision/language/global budget=44/16/4. Time projection and final FiLM weight
 start at zero; FiLM gate bias=log(.2/.8). Computation is BF16 for projections,
 FP32 for SSM/norm reductions/loss; trainable parameter storage stays FP32.

Differences from official Torch execution: JAX reference SSD rather than fused
 CUDA kernels, repository SigLIP/Gemma bridge without early exit, three cameras,
 58 actions over 50 frames, Pi05 time embedding and FM direction. All numerical
 comparisons align parameter layouts; none demonstrate fused-kernel parity.

Nonzero dense kernels use the repository NNX LeCun initializer rather than
Torch Linear Kaiming/MHA Xavier initializers; all new biases are zero except
FiLM gate bias. Parity tests transfer the same kernel values and account for
layouts; RNG/initial-weight parity with Torch is not claimed.

